  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=-{2}^{3x-4}+81.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-{2}^{3x-4}+81=0\n$$\n\nFirst, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by subtracting $81$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{2}^{3x-4}+81 & =0 \\\\ -{2}^{3x-4}+\\cancel{81}-\\cancel{81} & =0-81 \\\\ -{2}^{3x-4} & =-81 \\\\ {2}^{3x-4} & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite $81$ as ${3}^{4}$ to get\n\n$$\n{2}^{3x-4}={3}^{4}.\n$$\n\nThen we take ${log}_{2}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{3x-4} & ={3}^{4} \\\\ {log}_{2}\u2061({2}^{3x-4}) & ={log}_{2}\u2061({3}^{4}) \\\\ 3x-4 & =4{log}_{2}\u2061(3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-4 & =4{log}_{2}\u2061(3) \\\\ 3x & =4{log}_{2}\u2061(3)+4 \\\\ x & =\\frac{4{log}_{2}\u2061(3)+4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
